WEBVTT

01:34.729 --> 01:37.539
[Bloom Life]

01:38.479 --> 01:42.620
[2007]

01:41.479 --> 01:43.759
Look, two flocks of pigeons are racing.

01:44.479 --> 01:45.610
Look.

01:45.630 --> 01:47.430
Nur's flock is impressive!

01:47.460 --> 01:49.180
Will his pigeons win?

01:49.539 --> 01:51.700
Sadiq's tumbler pigeons

01:51.729 --> 01:53.270
are even better.

01:53.420 --> 01:55.400
Uncle Nur definitely won't win.

01:55.420 --> 01:57.280
That pigeon is flying towards us!

01:59.180 --> 02:01.580
What are you waiting for?
Let's go after it!

02:22.100 --> 02:24.079
Pigeons know the way home.

02:27.710 --> 02:28.530
Uncle.

02:30.370 --> 02:32.320
Grandma, Auntie.

02:32.470 --> 02:33.180
Look,

02:33.180 --> 02:35.800
you scared the dewdrops off my roses.

02:35.800 --> 02:38.610
Where are the dewdrops? Let me see.

02:54.610 --> 02:56.060
We finally caught it.

02:56.770 --> 02:58.930
It's so cute, all white.

03:06.470 --> 03:07.460
Arzugul.

03:07.520 --> 03:08.210
Laili?

03:10.750 --> 03:11.360
Come down.

03:12.590 --> 03:15.200
This is the pigeon
that flew away from the flock?

03:15.200 --> 03:16.360
You caught it?

03:27.050 --> 03:30.390
[Episode 6: The Home Won't Change]

03:44.860 --> 03:46.740
Why did you also plant a tree here?

03:46.740 --> 03:48.300
I just picked it up on the road.

03:48.300 --> 03:49.820
It looked half-dead.

03:50.210 --> 03:52.070
If I can save it, it's a life saved.

03:52.180 --> 03:53.340
Be careful.

03:53.340 --> 03:55.150
Planting a tree creates a bond.

03:55.150 --> 03:56.720
You have to water and fertilize it.

03:56.720 --> 03:58.780
I'm already running a homestay here.

03:58.870 --> 04:00.370
So I don't mind being "tied down" a bit.

04:00.370 --> 04:01.830
Didn't you plant one, too?

04:04.430 --> 04:05.630
This is my home.

04:05.870 --> 04:07.500
What's wrong with me planting one here?

04:07.500 --> 04:08.250
Besides,

04:08.250 --> 04:09.910
I might not stay here forever.

04:11.970 --> 04:12.550
Wait,

04:13.810 --> 04:15.310
you accepted my job offer,

04:15.500 --> 04:17.160
you can't just leave anytime.

04:28.190 --> 04:32.770
♪ My little sapling ♪

04:33.620 --> 04:34.409
So ugly.

04:43.070 --> 04:45.090
Laili.

04:45.120 --> 04:47.010
Ayisha, Cai, you're here.

04:47.040 --> 04:48.640
What do you want to eat today?

04:49.170 --> 04:49.909
What do you want to eat?

04:49.909 --> 04:53.090
-Fried chicken and yogurt.
-Fried chicken and yogurt.

04:53.110 --> 04:54.440
Okay, take a seat first.

04:55.400 --> 04:55.960
Let's go.

05:01.800 --> 05:03.030
Later, when Laili

05:03.390 --> 05:04.890
serves all our food,

05:04.890 --> 05:06.090
give her a heart sign

05:06.110 --> 05:07.170
when you thank her.

05:17.070 --> 05:18.000
The food is here.

05:18.190 --> 05:18.850
Let me help.

05:20.450 --> 05:23.550
-Thank you, Laili.
-Thank you, Laili.

05:23.800 --> 05:25.750
Who taught you that?

05:26.190 --> 05:27.630
We learned it ourselves.

05:27.630 --> 05:29.160
Yourselves? From whom?

05:36.860 --> 05:39.310
Is your instrument shop very free lately?

05:39.430 --> 05:41.270
Why does someone run two blocks every day

05:41.270 --> 05:42.510
just to buy chicken wings?

05:42.510 --> 05:43.400
No.

05:43.930 --> 05:44.790
It's these two.

05:45.070 --> 05:46.190
They said the food here is delicious

05:46.190 --> 05:47.630
and begged me to bring them.

05:47.630 --> 05:48.800
Right after lunch,

05:48.800 --> 05:51.250
Brother brought us here

05:51.270 --> 05:52.530
to eat.

05:52.920 --> 05:55.350
Brother burned the eggplants last night

05:55.430 --> 05:56.240
and mentioned Laili—

05:56.240 --> 05:57.390
Eat fried chicken.

06:00.680 --> 06:01.120
Laili.

06:01.800 --> 06:02.680
What's wrong?

06:05.920 --> 06:06.780
This is for you.

06:06.970 --> 06:07.900
Burn ointment.

06:07.990 --> 06:10.650
-We kept an extra for roasting lamb.
-Thank you.

06:14.820 --> 06:15.560
Here.

06:35.920 --> 06:37.040
When you apply it,

06:37.510 --> 06:38.680
go clockwise.

06:40.650 --> 06:41.710
You apply it for me.

06:55.350 --> 07:00.630
♪ Woods, oh poplar woods ♪

07:03.810 --> 07:04.890
What's wrong? What happened?

07:04.890 --> 07:06.060
That was so loud.

07:06.340 --> 07:07.450
What's wrong? What's that sound?

07:07.450 --> 07:08.250
What's wrong?

07:11.320 --> 07:12.260
What happened?

07:12.280 --> 07:14.280
Batur, what happened?

07:14.630 --> 07:15.490
The earth kiln.

07:16.000 --> 07:17.160
Don't just stand there.

07:17.160 --> 07:20.070
Throw water in it. Yes, throw it right in.

07:25.230 --> 07:26.760
I told you to watch the kiln.

07:27.730 --> 07:28.980
Where on earth did you go?

07:28.980 --> 07:29.680
I...

07:30.570 --> 07:31.680
Where did you go?

07:31.710 --> 07:32.680
I thought

07:32.680 --> 07:33.800
the temperature was stable,

07:33.800 --> 07:35.000
so I went out for a bit.

07:36.190 --> 07:38.190
You can't leave the kiln
while it's firing.

07:38.190 --> 07:40.060
Don't you know that?

07:40.980 --> 07:41.770
Ma'am.

07:43.070 --> 07:44.690
I heard that other earthenware shops

07:44.690 --> 07:45.360
installed electric kilns,

07:45.360 --> 07:46.920
so I wanted to take a look.

07:48.000 --> 07:49.680
Electric kilns fire fast and stably.

07:49.680 --> 07:50.830
And people don't have to

07:50.830 --> 07:52.159
watch them all the time.

07:52.570 --> 07:54.040
I even got the phone number

07:54.220 --> 07:56.130
of the electric kiln manufacturer.

07:56.130 --> 07:56.930
Master, look.

07:57.130 --> 07:58.730
Here is their business card.

07:59.280 --> 08:00.950
Master, electric kilns are really useful.

08:00.950 --> 08:01.630
Master!

08:02.180 --> 08:03.130
Since the kiln cracked,

08:03.130 --> 08:04.390
let's just replace it.

08:06.600 --> 08:07.360
Batur.

08:09.580 --> 08:10.510
Replace it?

08:12.680 --> 08:13.750
Do you have any idea

08:14.190 --> 08:15.390
just how important

08:16.000 --> 08:17.660
this ancient earthen kiln is?

08:19.800 --> 08:22.450
My great-grandfather

08:23.310 --> 08:24.240
left it behind.

08:24.240 --> 08:26.510
It's more precious to me than life itself.

08:26.510 --> 08:27.750
You, kid,

08:28.750 --> 08:30.010
are always looking for

08:30.410 --> 08:31.850
the easy way out.

08:32.650 --> 08:34.220
Haven't I told you

08:34.720 --> 08:35.669
that our family

08:36.120 --> 08:37.880
will never use those things?

08:38.169 --> 08:39.230
Do you understand?

08:42.250 --> 08:43.650
Other earthenware shops

08:45.030 --> 08:47.160
have more orders than they can handle.

08:49.080 --> 08:51.340
We're stuck with this broken earth kiln.

08:51.370 --> 08:52.970
How can we compete with them?

09:15.130 --> 09:15.840
Mom.

09:16.670 --> 09:18.670
How much does it cost to fix the kiln?

09:18.730 --> 09:21.380
I've got 400 saved up here.

09:21.410 --> 09:23.190
This is what's left from breakfast.

09:23.190 --> 09:24.560
-Mom, take it.
-No need.

09:24.790 --> 09:25.670
It will be fine.

09:25.720 --> 09:27.200
Trust me. It's really fine.

09:27.200 --> 09:29.320
I can get all the rest
of the money together.

09:29.320 --> 09:30.790
Our kiln will be fixed.

09:31.110 --> 09:32.640
I'll figure something out.

09:33.320 --> 09:33.820
This...

10:26.890 --> 10:27.770
Timur,

10:28.240 --> 10:31.760
have you ever seen a merlin
with your own eyes?

10:34.510 --> 10:36.960
They move so fast,

10:37.660 --> 10:40.180
catching little birds like a bullet.

10:41.890 --> 10:44.100
Sometimes I wonder,

10:48.770 --> 10:49.750
if

10:50.330 --> 10:54.040
my son Asimjan were still alive,

10:56.130 --> 10:57.460
would my daughter Laili

10:58.930 --> 11:03.660
still be as lively and active
as she is now,

11:04.700 --> 11:07.100
with the passion of a merlin?

11:09.180 --> 11:12.300
Maybe it's time to break the rule of passing it

11:13.340 --> 11:14.650
only to sons.

11:28.390 --> 11:30.150
Why can't you get the hang of it?

11:30.630 --> 11:33.270
The spout must be made higher.

11:33.670 --> 11:36.680
Otherwise, the water
will flow out with no pressure.

11:39.460 --> 11:41.260
Why are you just standing there?

11:43.580 --> 11:44.180
Come here.

11:45.280 --> 11:45.900
Come here.

11:54.250 --> 11:54.840
Come on,

11:55.330 --> 11:56.330
you try one.

12:00.650 --> 12:01.180
Come on.

12:03.980 --> 12:04.530
Do it.

12:10.610 --> 12:11.600
Slow down.

12:13.840 --> 12:14.410
Good.

12:14.830 --> 12:15.870
Very good.

12:18.270 --> 12:20.470
Families making earthenware like ours

12:21.540 --> 12:24.540
would originally only
pass the craft to sons.

12:25.170 --> 12:25.940
But

12:26.180 --> 12:29.710
you've loved making earthenware
so much since you were little.

12:30.250 --> 12:31.030
I have

12:31.600 --> 12:32.790
seen it all.

12:33.610 --> 12:34.520
Nowadays,

12:35.180 --> 12:38.830
more and more families
use machines to make earthenware.

12:41.000 --> 12:44.410
I want to teach you
the most traditional craft.

12:45.720 --> 12:47.440
Things made by machines

12:47.700 --> 12:48.660
are all the same

12:49.160 --> 12:50.250
and boring.

12:50.480 --> 12:52.850
Only handmade earthenware

12:52.980 --> 12:54.600
has warmth.

12:55.620 --> 12:57.250
I can't

12:58.390 --> 13:02.610
fully convey to you what it feels like

13:04.080 --> 13:06.240
to touch the clay.

13:06.890 --> 13:09.290
It all depends on your own understanding

13:09.290 --> 13:10.370
and effort.

13:15.240 --> 13:17.050
The water inside...

13:17.760 --> 13:19.590
It's dry. Oh, good.

13:41.030 --> 13:41.660
Dad.

13:44.120 --> 13:44.720
Dad.

13:46.630 --> 13:48.130
Why did you buy this?

13:49.200 --> 13:50.610
How can a girl like a flower

13:50.610 --> 13:53.140
have hands full of cracks?

13:54.960 --> 13:55.970
Dad, let me help you.

13:55.970 --> 13:56.610
No need.

13:56.700 --> 13:57.150
Give it to me.

13:57.150 --> 13:58.080
You go practice.

13:58.100 --> 13:59.160
And practice well,

13:59.630 --> 14:00.240
okay?

14:19.260 --> 14:20.620
Thank you, Zhou.

14:21.050 --> 14:23.810
You got all these hard-to-find paints
for me.

14:24.370 --> 14:25.390
You didn't have to deliver them in person.

14:25.390 --> 14:27.990
It's fine, Auntie. I was afraid they
might get damaged in transit.

14:27.990 --> 14:28.990
Don't mention it.

14:29.130 --> 14:30.230
After all, Xia Zi

14:30.840 --> 14:31.960
is my good friend.

14:35.150 --> 14:35.720
Zhou.

14:35.740 --> 14:36.420
Yes, Auntie.

14:36.420 --> 14:39.510
Let's not tell Xia Zi about this for now.

14:40.050 --> 14:42.310
I'm afraid she'll worry unnecessarily.

14:42.360 --> 14:44.080
Don't worry, I won't tell her.

15:20.480 --> 15:23.550
I'll sing a song I wrote myself.

15:24.080 --> 15:25.740
It's my first time singing it.

15:26.870 --> 15:27.720
Good!

15:41.600 --> 15:45.100
♪ The night sky tonight ♪

15:45.410 --> 15:48.410
♪ Is filled with beautiful dreams ♪

15:48.980 --> 15:52.580
♪ In the grass of the valley ♪

15:52.610 --> 15:56.150
♪ Who hid away time and space ♪

15:56.420 --> 16:00.150
♪ Those long, lingering memories ♪

16:00.170 --> 16:03.940
♪ Are so captivating ♪

16:03.960 --> 16:07.550
♪ Searching for the lost self ♪

16:07.650 --> 16:11.650
♪ What was it that you threw into time ♪

16:11.670 --> 16:16.910
♪ What is it that can define you and me ♪

16:19.630 --> 16:26.810
♪ Laili ♪

16:27.480 --> 16:33.460
♪ Laili ♪

16:42.200 --> 16:44.600
I didn't expect you
to write your own songs.

16:46.320 --> 16:48.000
Music is all connected.

16:48.290 --> 16:51.240
And Grandpa also wants me
to learn more things.

16:51.620 --> 16:54.620
Actually, I've always wanted
to compose my own music.

16:55.250 --> 16:56.390
Actually, me too.

16:57.700 --> 17:01.030
I think besides those traditional jars,

17:01.030 --> 17:02.600
I also want to make some

17:02.600 --> 17:03.840
different things,

17:03.990 --> 17:07.030
like putting my feelings

17:07.180 --> 17:08.510
or my mood

17:08.510 --> 17:09.700
into the clay.

17:09.700 --> 17:11.200
I think it would be different.

17:11.200 --> 17:12.230
Definitely.

17:12.500 --> 17:15.060
And I believe you can do it.

17:17.270 --> 17:18.569
Also, right now,

17:18.920 --> 17:21.030
I have some motifs in my head.

17:21.640 --> 17:24.750
A melody keeps playing in my mind.

17:24.950 --> 17:26.119
-Do you want to hear it?
-What melody?

17:26.119 --> 17:27.020
Yes.

17:27.060 --> 17:27.770
Then I'll play it for you.

17:27.770 --> 17:28.170
Okay.

18:48.750 --> 18:49.860
What time is it?

18:49.880 --> 18:51.020
Why are you singing?

18:51.200 --> 18:53.400
Are you going to let people sleep or not?

19:06.640 --> 19:07.480
You go first.

19:11.510 --> 19:14.140
I actually have 2 pieces
of good news for you.

19:14.510 --> 19:15.240
Tell me.

19:16.090 --> 19:17.690
The first bit of good news...

19:21.240 --> 19:22.640
Is it that funny?

19:24.180 --> 19:25.710
I'm telling you seriously.

19:26.290 --> 19:27.350
The first bit of good news

19:27.350 --> 19:30.550
is that my father finally
agreed to teach me earthenware.

19:30.710 --> 19:31.910
That's great!

19:32.250 --> 19:33.980
The second piece of good news is

19:35.200 --> 19:37.000
that now that I'm learning
the earthenware,

19:37.000 --> 19:39.200
I don't have to marry Mulading anymore.

19:43.210 --> 19:44.470
So you are off the hook.

19:57.020 --> 19:58.880
But I don't want to be off the hook.

20:11.920 --> 20:12.960
I like you.

20:15.640 --> 20:17.170
I want to be your boyfriend.

20:17.680 --> 20:18.810
This time, I mean it.

20:18.980 --> 20:20.110
No more pretending.

20:24.420 --> 20:25.500
But...

20:26.930 --> 20:29.200
I'm not as pretty as Minawar.

20:29.840 --> 20:31.840
And I'm not as smart as Arzugul.

20:32.720 --> 20:34.050
I feel like I...

20:34.050 --> 20:35.430
Grandpa told me,

20:36.500 --> 20:38.310
"Choose a lover with your heart,

20:38.590 --> 20:39.510
not your eyes."

20:40.590 --> 20:42.250
I just like you the way you are.

20:46.640 --> 20:47.770
I like you, too.

20:49.590 --> 20:50.330
What?

20:51.480 --> 20:52.680
What did you just say?

20:52.700 --> 20:54.090
I... I said I like you too.

20:54.090 --> 20:54.890
Say it again.

20:55.550 --> 20:56.750
Say it a bit louder.

20:56.750 --> 20:58.420
I said I like you too!

20:58.680 --> 20:59.610
What did you say?

20:59.880 --> 21:00.500
I said—

21:00.500 --> 21:02.010
You what?

21:02.680 --> 21:03.480
What?

21:03.480 --> 21:05.200
She said she likes you, too!

21:05.230 --> 21:07.410
♪ Girl, oh girl ♪

21:07.440 --> 21:09.300
♪ Listen to a few words from me ♪

21:08.240 --> 21:09.670
I like you.

21:09.330 --> 21:11.900
♪ Could you please leave me ♪

21:11.940 --> 21:13.800
♪ Your QQ number ♪

21:13.830 --> 21:16.390
♪ If you are a big dinosaur ♪

21:16.410 --> 21:18.120
♪ I'll be a little frog too ♪

21:18.140 --> 21:20.800
♪ Let's not look down on each other ♪

21:20.830 --> 21:27.300
♪ Let's just be friends ♪

21:28.020 --> 21:45.580
♪ Darling, come on, come on, come on ♪

22:19.840 --> 22:21.420
Grandma went out in the afternoon.

22:21.420 --> 22:23.050
She hasn't come back yet.

22:23.200 --> 22:24.290
Mom!

22:25.660 --> 22:26.220
Mom!

22:26.220 --> 22:26.980
You look over there.

22:26.980 --> 22:28.040
I'll look this way.

22:29.980 --> 22:31.050
Grandma!

22:33.240 --> 22:34.590
Grandma.

22:41.090 --> 22:41.960
Grandma.

22:46.480 --> 22:47.410
Grandma.

22:48.240 --> 22:50.550
Why are you here?

22:51.820 --> 22:56.600
I'm here waiting
for your grandpa to come home.

22:57.120 --> 22:58.580
Your grandpa

22:58.600 --> 23:01.530
went to Yarkant to collect taxes.

23:02.090 --> 23:04.110
He was riding a horse,

23:04.430 --> 23:06.370
carrying a hunting rifle.

23:07.780 --> 23:09.990
How handsome he was.

23:10.400 --> 23:11.620
In a few days,

23:11.880 --> 23:13.240
he will come back.

23:14.350 --> 23:15.660
I wonder if he returns,

23:16.140 --> 23:18.660
will he be able to find our home?

23:22.880 --> 23:24.070
Grandma.

23:24.810 --> 23:27.550
Our home is over there.

23:28.830 --> 23:29.850
No.

23:29.880 --> 23:31.960
This is our house.

23:33.240 --> 23:34.750
Look.

23:34.750 --> 23:37.810
Isn't this pattern different from ours?

23:39.720 --> 23:42.170
The color is the same,

23:42.250 --> 23:44.480
but the pattern has changed.

23:44.500 --> 23:45.900
If my husband comes back,

23:46.240 --> 23:49.090
can he find our home?

23:53.260 --> 23:55.830
When your grandfather comes back,

23:55.860 --> 24:01.420
I'm worried he won't find his way home.

24:03.590 --> 24:06.750
What if he can't find home?

24:10.440 --> 24:11.650
Grandma's words

24:12.280 --> 24:15.740
made me think about the direction
of the homestay renovation.

24:16.010 --> 24:17.410
The carvings on the gate,

24:18.210 --> 24:19.650
the smell of figs,

24:20.430 --> 24:21.890
and the touch of old things

24:23.170 --> 24:25.100
all help a wandering little pigeon

24:26.160 --> 24:28.030
recognize the way home.

25:53.330 --> 25:54.200
Hurry up.

25:54.200 --> 25:55.530
The mooncakes are here.

25:56.900 --> 25:58.670
Aunt Chang Yue bought these
especially for us.

25:58.670 --> 26:00.470
Come on, everyone, have a taste.

26:00.570 --> 26:01.620
Come on.

26:01.810 --> 26:05.170
It's the Mid-Autumn Festival.
How can we not have mooncakes?

26:05.170 --> 26:05.950
Chang Yue.

26:06.390 --> 26:08.770
You haven't been
to our house for a long time.

26:08.770 --> 26:09.770
Come have a taste.

26:09.980 --> 26:10.700
Mom.

26:11.250 --> 26:13.010
Aunt Jiang told you
to avoid "trigger" foods

26:13.010 --> 26:14.410
and eat more vegetables.

26:14.440 --> 26:15.640
It's a holiday today.

26:15.660 --> 26:17.420
If Auntie wants to eat it,
let her have more.

26:17.420 --> 26:18.530
Why are you giving her more?

26:18.530 --> 26:19.140
Don't listen to her.

26:19.140 --> 26:20.200
Leave my mom alone.

26:20.460 --> 26:21.400
Come on.

26:21.400 --> 26:22.140
Everyone, eat.

26:22.140 --> 26:23.470
Everyone, have a taste.

26:23.530 --> 26:24.260
You try some.

26:25.380 --> 26:26.600
Come on, eat.

26:26.630 --> 26:27.480
Come on, everyone, eat.

26:27.480 --> 26:28.740
Eat while it's hot.

26:29.700 --> 26:31.210
While everyone is gathered here,

26:31.210 --> 26:33.470
I have some good news to share.

26:36.570 --> 26:38.010
Our old inn

26:38.010 --> 26:40.050
has been running for many years.

26:40.510 --> 26:42.680
I have spent most of my life here.

26:42.940 --> 26:45.610
My great-great-grandfather

26:45.610 --> 26:47.270
was also born in this house.

26:47.270 --> 26:48.640
When my dad was young,

26:48.640 --> 26:50.270
he renovated it

26:50.270 --> 26:51.660
a bit.

26:52.510 --> 26:53.690
No one

26:54.330 --> 26:56.130
loves this place more than we do.

26:57.090 --> 26:58.170
As everyone knows,

26:58.200 --> 27:00.050
our century-old house

27:00.070 --> 27:01.750
can't keep up
with the outside development now.

27:01.750 --> 27:03.150
If we just wait like this,

27:03.580 --> 27:05.010
I'm afraid it

27:05.040 --> 27:06.650
will be ruined in my hands.

27:13.460 --> 27:14.520
It's so beautiful.

27:14.530 --> 27:15.720
So pretty.

27:15.940 --> 27:16.570
This is

27:16.590 --> 27:20.090
a gift from me to Grandma and everyone.

27:20.410 --> 27:22.070
The blueprint for the new inn.

27:22.310 --> 27:23.050
Come, let me see.

27:23.050 --> 27:23.510
Auntie.

27:24.420 --> 27:25.030
Look how nice the design is.

27:25.030 --> 27:26.090
It's so beautiful.

27:26.740 --> 27:28.610
Dad, our house is in there, too.

27:29.290 --> 27:31.290
Why does this look so familiar to me?

27:32.310 --> 27:34.110
This is a sketch
I've been working on lately.

27:34.110 --> 27:35.790
I made some changes

27:35.790 --> 27:37.240
to the internal structure,

27:37.240 --> 27:38.770
but the exterior is essentially
a recreation

27:38.770 --> 27:40.680
of how it looked back in Grandpa's day.

27:40.680 --> 27:41.740
That way,

27:41.740 --> 27:44.830
Grandpa will never
lose his way home again.

27:45.660 --> 27:46.590
Grandma.

27:47.110 --> 27:48.560
The home won't change.

27:48.840 --> 27:50.020
Please don't worry.

27:51.450 --> 27:53.480
The home won't change.

27:54.030 --> 27:56.550
The home really won't change.

28:02.110 --> 28:03.310
Does Grandma like it?

28:03.410 --> 28:04.480
Yes.

28:04.600 --> 28:06.530
She said, "The home won't change."

28:32.770 --> 28:33.870
What are you doing

28:33.890 --> 28:35.000
sneaking around?

28:40.290 --> 28:42.020
Let me show you some good stuff.

28:44.650 --> 28:45.610
Hey.

28:46.560 --> 28:48.440
Why did you withdraw so much money?

28:48.440 --> 28:50.300
We're starting work soon, right?

28:50.680 --> 28:52.090
What the workers care about most

28:52.090 --> 28:52.920
is this:

28:53.000 --> 28:54.700
solid cash.

28:56.290 --> 28:58.820
I find you're becoming
more and more like a Kashgar local.

28:58.820 --> 29:00.680
Have you ever heard a saying here?

29:01.330 --> 29:02.610
How much do Kashgar people

29:02.610 --> 29:04.400
love doing business?

29:04.420 --> 29:05.830
Even if there's only one person,

29:05.830 --> 29:08.760
they'd sell things from their left pocket
to their right pocket.

29:08.760 --> 29:09.680
It's...

29:09.700 --> 29:12.500
They don't care about the result,
but the process.

29:27.960 --> 29:29.900
As the inn's renovation begins,

29:30.530 --> 29:31.530
everyone's heart

29:32.140 --> 29:33.140
flutters with it.

29:35.520 --> 29:36.850
Amidst the reluctance,

29:37.030 --> 29:38.760
it is also full of expectation.

29:40.530 --> 29:41.270
This century-old house embedded in

29:41.270 --> 29:43.640
everyone's memory

29:45.590 --> 29:46.680
will also welcome

29:47.020 --> 29:48.760
its new life cycle.

30:30.380 --> 30:32.510
Forty days have passed
in the blink of an eye.

30:32.510 --> 30:34.110
She grows so fast.

30:34.280 --> 30:35.720
So beautiful. Looks exactly like you.

30:35.720 --> 30:36.240
Really?

30:36.240 --> 30:37.140
Yes.

30:39.440 --> 30:40.290
Come.

30:40.660 --> 30:41.850
Let Grandma hold you.

30:41.850 --> 30:42.900
Thanks for your hard work, child.

30:42.900 --> 30:44.070
No, no.

30:45.160 --> 30:46.840
Let Grandma hold you.

30:46.870 --> 30:48.190
Let me hold you.

30:48.960 --> 30:50.240
Let me hold you.

30:52.570 --> 30:53.570
Come.

30:55.880 --> 30:56.790
Come.

30:57.170 --> 30:58.530
Use golden water

30:58.560 --> 31:00.830
to wash our baby's hands.

31:05.160 --> 31:05.940
Little feet.

31:05.940 --> 31:07.320
Wash the little feet.

31:07.350 --> 31:08.680
Little feet. All right.

31:08.680 --> 31:09.220
Come,

31:09.570 --> 31:11.070
Minawar,

31:11.200 --> 31:11.720
look.

31:11.980 --> 31:15.740
This is a gift
for my eldest granddaughter.

31:17.660 --> 31:18.640
About this...

31:20.220 --> 31:21.220
Next year,

31:21.440 --> 31:24.010
when you give me a big,
healthy baby boy...

31:24.010 --> 31:25.140
I'll keep it for him.

31:29.550 --> 31:31.180
Let Auntie hold you.

31:31.790 --> 31:32.720
So cute.

31:32.720 --> 31:34.780
Her eyes look just like my brother's.

31:36.310 --> 31:36.880
Come.

31:36.880 --> 31:37.750
Is the baby sleepy?

31:37.750 --> 31:39.180
Here, let me take her.

31:40.180 --> 31:41.580
When Minawar was little,

31:41.790 --> 31:43.770
as soon as she heard my lullabies,

31:44.030 --> 31:45.430
she would sleep soundly.

31:46.200 --> 31:47.440
Yes, yes.

31:47.790 --> 31:52.530
♪ Sleep, my baby, sleep, my baby ♪

31:52.550 --> 31:56.070
♪ Sleep, my baby ♪

31:56.120 --> 32:00.580
♪ Sleep, my baby, sleep, my baby ♪

32:00.740 --> 32:05.540
♪ Sleep, my baby, sleep, my baby ♪

32:06.360 --> 32:13.570
♪ Sleep, my baby, sleep, my baby ♪

32:14.150 --> 32:21.320
♪ Sleep, my baby, sleep, my baby ♪

32:23.340 --> 32:24.600
Come, eat this.

32:24.770 --> 32:25.180
Gangzi meat.

32:25.180 --> 32:25.600
Eat.

32:27.530 --> 32:28.750
Careful, it's hot.

32:30.120 --> 32:32.660
We are already way over budget.

32:33.570 --> 32:34.970
Let me do the math for you.

32:35.440 --> 32:37.400
Now the doors, windows, stairs,

32:37.610 --> 32:39.030
and other decorations—

32:39.500 --> 32:41.380
Based on their current efficiency,

32:41.380 --> 32:43.840
they won't be able
to finish it in half a year.

32:43.840 --> 32:45.010
For the next six months,

32:45.010 --> 32:46.730
we can't just spend money
without making any.

32:46.730 --> 32:47.710
These masters

32:47.840 --> 32:48.970
do work a bit slowly.

32:49.030 --> 32:51.030
But slow work yields fine products.

32:51.900 --> 32:52.570
Think about it,

32:52.570 --> 32:53.750
which skilled master

32:53.750 --> 32:54.790
doesn't have a temper,

32:54.790 --> 32:55.680
right?

32:56.400 --> 32:58.480
These pillars are
different from other things.

32:58.480 --> 32:59.940
They will be with this house for decades,

32:59.940 --> 33:01.310
or even centuries.

33:01.960 --> 33:03.000
And for our homestay,

33:03.000 --> 33:04.350
it's the woodwork that gives
the place its soul.

33:04.350 --> 33:05.160
We must wait

33:05.160 --> 33:06.960
for this.

33:08.030 --> 33:08.920
At worst,

33:08.920 --> 33:10.000
when laying the tiles,

33:10.000 --> 33:11.730
we can make up for the lost time.

33:13.640 --> 33:14.140
Boss,

33:15.180 --> 33:16.090
we are off work.

33:17.240 --> 33:17.980
Okay.

33:17.980 --> 33:19.110
Thanks for your hard work.

33:19.110 --> 33:20.250
See you tomorrow.

33:20.250 --> 33:20.850
Alright.

33:23.750 --> 33:24.940
Where are you going?

33:24.940 --> 33:26.090
Having dinner with my mom.

33:26.090 --> 33:27.090
You can eat this.

33:28.000 --> 33:29.240
Well, you're going

33:29.240 --> 33:30.510
to see Auntie?

33:33.330 --> 33:34.930
Auntie, Xia Zi is going home.

33:35.050 --> 33:37.310
You should pack up those things quickly.

33:43.160 --> 33:43.720
Who is it?

33:43.720 --> 33:45.270
W-Why are you back?

33:46.310 --> 33:48.840
Don't you want me
to come back and eat with you?

33:51.500 --> 33:53.110
I'm super hungry today.

33:53.110 --> 33:54.090
Cook more noodles.

33:54.090 --> 33:55.380
Whatever.

33:55.380 --> 33:56.160
Anything is fine.

33:56.160 --> 33:56.920
Okay.

34:22.230 --> 34:24.300
What are you doing in such a hurry?

34:25.800 --> 34:27.400
What are you packing?

34:30.440 --> 34:32.300
I never had the chance to tell you.

34:33.030 --> 34:34.280
I applied to go to

34:34.860 --> 34:36.460
the Kizil Cave Institute

34:36.630 --> 34:37.730
as a volunteer

34:37.730 --> 34:38.920
to copy murals.

34:40.190 --> 34:41.590
You are leaving Kashgar?

34:46.130 --> 34:47.530
Are you selling the wood?

34:48.980 --> 34:51.190
Stop bargaining.
Let's settle it like this.

34:51.190 --> 34:52.590
Load the truck quickly.

34:53.000 --> 34:54.980
We'll still do business in the future.

34:54.980 --> 34:57.040
We are friends. Don't talk like that.

35:00.000 --> 35:01.230
It has to be my mom.

35:01.230 --> 35:03.160
She always manages to surprise me.

35:03.170 --> 35:04.550
She has been

35:04.550 --> 35:06.080
planning it for a long time.

35:07.190 --> 35:09.130
She was worried you'd feel too lonely

35:09.130 --> 35:10.730
being on your own in Kashgar.

35:12.530 --> 35:14.660
You knew about this earlier than I did.

35:16.670 --> 35:18.230
She told me not to tell you.

35:18.400 --> 35:20.340
When I helped her
buy paint last time,

35:20.340 --> 35:22.000
she told me to keep it a secret.

35:22.440 --> 35:23.440
I was afraid you'd worry

35:23.440 --> 35:24.880
about her heart

35:24.880 --> 35:25.880
and health.

35:26.190 --> 35:27.880
I was just thinking of you.

35:31.880 --> 35:32.940
Tell me,

35:33.530 --> 35:35.650
when did we start

35:37.050 --> 35:39.230
looking out for each other like this?

35:46.960 --> 35:48.860
You know, for the neck

35:49.760 --> 35:51.260
of the instruments we make,

35:51.260 --> 35:53.110
we use "male" wood.

35:53.880 --> 35:55.320
"Male," as in male and female.

35:55.320 --> 35:56.210
They are divided into male and female?

35:56.210 --> 35:57.960
Yes, male.

35:58.190 --> 35:59.280
Look, hold it like this.

35:59.280 --> 36:00.360
If you want to grab it, do this.

36:00.360 --> 36:01.110
Like this.

36:01.280 --> 36:03.400
Because the male one is harder,

36:03.400 --> 36:04.440
and the female one is softer.

36:04.440 --> 36:06.170
They match better for the tone.

36:06.590 --> 36:09.050
I feel that making earthenware is easier.

36:09.050 --> 36:10.590
The clay is soft,

36:10.590 --> 36:11.670
unlike this wood—

36:12.760 --> 36:14.170
It's rock hard.

36:22.460 --> 36:23.480
I give up.

36:23.670 --> 36:24.920
I'm telling you,

36:25.150 --> 36:26.400
it's these woods

36:26.840 --> 36:28.900
that make the most beautiful sounds.

36:29.510 --> 36:31.770
Then why do you like making instruments?

36:32.510 --> 36:35.710
My family has been making instruments
for 7 generations.

36:35.880 --> 36:37.960
So I was born to make instruments.

36:38.710 --> 36:39.980
When I was young,

36:40.320 --> 36:41.670
I was actually very envious

36:41.670 --> 36:44.530
of kids who could play football
right after school.

36:44.940 --> 36:45.960
Until I was...

36:46.500 --> 36:47.110
thir...

36:47.110 --> 36:47.380
right,

36:47.380 --> 36:48.550
thirteen years old.

36:49.070 --> 36:50.960
I made my first instrument.

36:51.710 --> 36:54.110
When I plucked the string like this

36:54.670 --> 36:56.110
and heard it hum,

36:57.920 --> 37:00.550
I felt like the whole world
had settled down.

37:01.280 --> 37:02.710
I understand that feeling.

37:02.710 --> 37:03.550
It's like

37:03.780 --> 37:05.300
suddenly your eyes

37:05.300 --> 37:06.670
really opened,

37:06.670 --> 37:08.840
and the whole world became bright.

37:08.840 --> 37:09.960
It's like

37:09.960 --> 37:10.940
I know

37:11.320 --> 37:12.710
where I can go,

37:13.000 --> 37:14.320
and where I will go.

37:14.920 --> 37:16.860
Every time I make earthenware,

37:17.190 --> 37:18.880
I feel like

37:18.880 --> 37:20.190
I'm no longer Laili.

37:20.190 --> 37:21.840
I become a different Laili.

37:22.840 --> 37:23.710
I became

37:23.710 --> 37:24.920
stronger,

37:24.920 --> 37:26.130
calmer,

37:26.130 --> 37:27.480
undisturbed,

37:27.480 --> 37:28.710
and more focused.

37:30.460 --> 37:31.920
Then you should be bolder,

37:32.210 --> 37:34.140
and go create work that's your own.

37:35.610 --> 37:36.860
Do you remember the song

37:36.860 --> 37:38.460
I sang in the alley last time?

37:38.840 --> 37:39.820
I've finished writing it.

37:39.820 --> 37:40.860
Finished?

38:02.580 --> 38:07.140
♪ We are lonely souls ♪

38:09.420 --> 38:14.590
♪ Drifting in and out of the crowds ♪

38:15.850 --> 38:21.520
♪ Confining dusk within the dawn ♪

38:22.590 --> 38:27.270
♪ Waiting aimlessly
for the traffic lights ♪

38:29.180 --> 38:34.520
♪ Suddenly, I never ask again ♪

38:35.620 --> 38:41.030
♪ About the lingering warmth upon waking ♪

38:41.870 --> 38:48.020
♪ This unexpected sincerity ♪

38:44.980 --> 38:46.580
Aren't we just good friends?

38:49.060 --> 38:54.270
♪ Makes each of our lives complete ♪

38:52.070 --> 38:53.130
Ordinary friends.

38:55.130 --> 39:02.020
♪ I can't quite describe it ♪

38:59.540 --> 39:01.000
Long live our friendship.

39:02.290 --> 39:05.470
♪ A sudden, unexpected surprise ♪

39:05.540 --> 39:08.520
♪ Don't go away too fast ♪

39:08.550 --> 39:15.260
♪ It truly exists ♪

39:15.280 --> 39:18.910
♪ Thank you for your generosity ♪

39:18.930 --> 39:23.640
♪ For making me believe in love ♪

39:32.180 --> 39:37.510
♪ We are the lucky ones ♪

39:34.320 --> 39:35.880
I think this material is really good.

39:35.880 --> 39:37.610
It's perfect for our homestay.

39:38.420 --> 39:39.360
Take a look.

39:38.940 --> 39:44.450
♪ Mixed with complicated feelings
at times ♪

39:43.880 --> 39:44.550
This one?

39:45.230 --> 39:45.960
I think it's okay.

39:45.960 --> 39:47.510
We can put it at the doorplate.

39:46.070 --> 39:51.760
♪ The mornings we wake up together ♪

39:47.510 --> 39:49.640
I feel like this one's not quite right.

39:50.530 --> 39:52.170
If you think it's not right,
why call me over?

39:52.170 --> 39:58.070
♪ Often leave me staring
at you in a daze ♪

39:53.400 --> 39:55.000
You take a look for yourself.

39:58.370 --> 40:05.570
♪ I can't quite describe it ♪

39:59.500 --> 40:00.710
Xia Zi,

40:00.710 --> 40:03.400
what do you think of Zhou?

40:03.400 --> 40:06.000
Mom, it's been ages
since I've even been in a relationship.

40:05.860 --> 40:09.200
♪ A sudden, unexpected surprise ♪

40:06.400 --> 40:08.940
I haven't even figured out
my own life yet.

40:08.940 --> 40:11.070
How can I start with someone else?

40:09.230 --> 40:11.690
♪ Don't go away too fast ♪

40:11.760 --> 40:18.730
♪ It truly exists ♪

40:14.590 --> 40:16.170
Does this fig

40:17.050 --> 40:18.960
have a heart

40:18.760 --> 40:21.890
♪ Thank you for your generosity ♪

40:19.300 --> 40:21.030
or not?

40:22.060 --> 40:27.740
♪ For making me believe in love ♪

40:43.860 --> 40:47.090
An extra 320,000.

40:59.340 --> 41:00.340
I'll...

41:00.840 --> 41:02.100
go back to my hometown.

41:05.840 --> 41:06.960
For how long?

41:10.800 --> 41:12.000
I don't know, either.

41:14.610 --> 41:16.140
I need to raise money first.

41:17.110 --> 41:18.730
Only after tearing the place down

41:18.730 --> 41:21.990
did we realize the drainage
and gas lines all need redoing—

41:22.030 --> 41:23.110
oh, and...

41:24.150 --> 41:26.350
the water and electrical systems, too.

41:26.610 --> 41:27.950
I'll go back first.

41:28.340 --> 41:30.380
We'll pause the construction here for now.

41:30.380 --> 41:32.490
I'll rush back as soon as I get the money.

41:32.490 --> 41:34.930
Please take good care of my sapling.

41:35.610 --> 41:37.130
Oh, don't worry.

41:37.130 --> 41:39.510
I'll water it when I water mine.

41:41.370 --> 41:43.170
What's there to worry about?

41:52.830 --> 41:55.250
Congratulations on your
honorable retirement, Dr. Chang.

41:55.250 --> 41:56.450
Thank you, Director.

42:31.360 --> 42:32.250
Thank you.

42:32.670 --> 42:33.970
Thank you, everyone.

42:35.380 --> 42:36.820
Thank you, everyone.

42:39.050 --> 42:40.010
Thank you.

42:40.860 --> 42:41.880
Dr. Chang.

42:42.800 --> 42:45.030
Congratulations on your retirement.

42:52.420 --> 42:53.380
May you

42:53.820 --> 42:54.950
unburden yourself,

42:55.610 --> 42:57.340
start your new chapter afresh,

42:57.840 --> 42:59.340
and find your inner path.
